= Abstract
We will introduce version control generally, and Git and GitHub specifically.
It will be a very hands-on session so make sure to bring a laptop with Git set up.
If you're not sure how to install and set up Git there is a guide available at https://macconville.ie/masterclass.
We will also ensure at the start of the session that everyone has a functioning system.
We will cover all the essentials, from pushing and pulling to setting up remotes and collaborating.
It will all be accompanied by practical exercises to work along with.
Time permitting, we will also look at some GitHub specific features.
Notes, slides, and follow-up reading for those who wish to go further will all be provided.
